{"author": "ValWood", "body": "* **ARBA rule (ID and label):**\n\n\nGO:0006465 | signal peptide processing | IEA with ARBA00085772\n\n* **Sequences with problematic annotation (ID + gene/protein name):**\n\nhttps://www.pombase.org/gene/SPBC543.09\n\n* **Description of issue**\n\nThe m-AAA complex acts after initial import and MTS cleavage, and within the inner membrane, rather than in the matrix or intermembrane space.\n\nIn some specific cases, the m-AAA complex may process transmembrane proteins that require internal cleavage for function (e.g., MRPL32, a ribosomal subunit), but this is not the same as classical N-terminal signal peptide removal.", "created_at": "2025-06-21T14:56:18Z", "key": "issue", "labels": ["ARBA", "ARBA - checked", "mitochondrion"], "state": "closed", "state_reason": "completed", "title": "GO:0006465\t signal peptide processing IEA with ARBA00085772", "type": "issue", "updated_at": "2026-08-07T11:47:59Z"}
